TIP:  For the intro, in each pairing first form the chord in the pair and then rake (arpeggio) the strings at and below that level.  For example, (a) - (A) means form the (A) and strum strings 3 - 2 - 1 while holding the (A).  Then you'd form (A7) and strum strings 3 - 2 - 1.  And so forth.  For (d) - (Dm) you'd form (Dm) and rake strings 4 - 3 - 2 - 1, and for (b) - (E7) form (E7) and rake strings 5 - 4 - 3 - 2 - 1.
 
TIP:  (C#m) is just (Bm) played on the 4th fret.

TIP:  Not too fast.


